  "vendor_profiles": {
    "$note": "Vendor -> item-kind affinity. A pharmacy does not sell a personalised nutrition plan, and until this block existed nothing stopped it from printing one. Each profile lists every item kind an outlet of that sort can put on a line, across all three policy buckets; the item kinds are the vocabulary of config/policy.yaml and a profile naming one that no category declares is a typo the test suite catches. A vendor carries a profile slug rather than its own list because outlets of the same sort sell the same things — the affinity is a property of the trade, not of the shop.",
    "$note_coverage": "A profile that intersects a category's covered_items can issue a receipt for that category at all; one that also intersects its excluded_items can carry a MIXED basket. The assembler picks a vendor that can carry the plan rather than letting the builder fail on a vendor that never could.",
    "$note_reachability": "Two invariants the test suite enforces, both about content that would otherwise vanish or leak without saying so. FIRST: every item kind policy.yaml declares must be sold by some profile, or it is silently absent from every dataset this generator produces. SECOND: every COVERED kind must be sold by at least one profile that also sells something the same category excludes — otherwise a line printing that kind is guaranteed never to appear on a partially-covered document, and the line item alone foretells the label. Some profiles are still covered-only on their own (`private_tutor`, `online_learning_platform`); that is a residual leak on the counterparty, recorded under `known_limitations` in config/labelling-schema.yaml.",

    "insurer": ["insurance_premium", "family_member_premium", "property_insurance", "travel_insurance"],

    "language_school": ["language_lessons", "placement_test", "language_exam", "missed_lesson_fee", "textbook", "stationery"],
    "private_tutor": ["language_lessons", "placement_test", "missed_lesson_fee"],
    "exam_centre": ["language_exam", "placement_test", "textbook"],

